---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Methodology | Nordic Systems" description="How Nordic Systems distinguishes sources, inference, and speculation in architecture maps.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20 lg:px-8">
    <header class="page-intro max-w-3xl">
      <p class="page-kicker">Methodology</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.08] tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">
        Evidence, separated by confidence.
      </h1>
      <p class="page-lead mt-6">
        Nordic Systems creates original reconstructions of architecture from public material. We do
        not claim that a company’s architecture is verified by the company unless a source explicitly
        supports a specific claim.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="claim-statuses-heading">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4 border-b border-slate-200 pb-4">
        <div>
          <p class="page-kicker">Evidence labels</p>
          <h2 id="claim-statuses-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
            Claim statuses
          </h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <dl class="method-status-list mt-6">
        <div class="method-status method-status--documented">
          <span class="method-status__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <dt>Documented</dt>
            <dd>A claim linked to at least one public source.</dd>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="method-status method-status--inferred">
          <span class="method-status__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <dt>Inferred</dt>
            <dd>A reasoned interpretation. Its rationale is included so readers can assess it.</dd>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="method-status method-status--speculative">
          <span class="method-status__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div>
            <dt>Speculative</dt>
            <dd>A possibility that lacks enough evidence to present as an inference or fact.</dd>
          </div>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-x-16 gap-y-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="confidence-heading">
        <p class="page-kicker">Confidence and time</p>
        <h2 id="confidence-heading" class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
          Read claims in context
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700">
          Confidence describes how strongly the available evidence supports a claim; it is not a
          guarantee. As-of dates state the latest time the claim is intended to represent. Claims
          older than three years receive a “May be outdated” warning, including when only a year or
          month is known.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="method-section" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
        <p class="page-kicker">Sources and original work</p>
        <h2 id="sources-heading" class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
          Trace every statement
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm leading-7 text-slate-700">
          We choose public engineering posts, talks, documentation, and open-source material that
          directly help support a claim. When an archived URL is available, we link it alongside the
          original. Summaries and diagrams are written and drawn by Nordic Systems; we do not copy
          source text or diagrams.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="method-correction mt-16" aria-labelledby="correction-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="page-kicker">Corrections</p>
        <h2 id="correction-heading" class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
          Found a source issue?
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
          If a source is missing, stale, or misread, share the relevant public evidence.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a
        class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-slate-900 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-slate-700 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sky-700"
        href="https://github.com/mehmood14/nordic-systems/issues"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Open a GitHub issue
      </a>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
